  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that NU1025 may interact with Sodium/Potassium Transporting ATPase subunits through its targets, which include Cytochrome c4 and other compounds. These targets are implicated in the regulation of ion transport, a critical function of the Sodium/Potassium Transporting ATPase subunits. The scores from the paths indicate a moderate level of confidence in the relationship, with some evidence pointing to multiple compounds acting as intermediaries in this interaction. The presence of multiple targets, including different chemical structures, suggests a potential mechanism involving the modulation of ion transport activity through various molecular pathways. The evidence is consistent with the idea that NU1025 may influence the function of these ATPase subunits, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct interaction.",
